  "Monetary values are in the cost currency of the network data; PyPSA stores no currency unit, GridStorm assumes EUR (example-network costs are illustrative, not market data).",
  "capex_installed_eur = nominal capacity (p_nom/s_nom/e_nom) x capital_cost (PyPSA statistics.installed_capex); available without optimisation.",
  "capex_optimal_eur = optimal capacity (*_opt) x capital_cost (PyPSA statistics.capex, the quantity PyPSA-Explorer plots); null when the network is not solved.",
  "opex_eur = dispatch x marginal cost (plus storage/spill/unit-commitment cost terms when present) weighted by snapshot_weightings.objective (PyPSA statistics.opex); null when the network is not solved.",
  "capital_cost is the model's per-period (typically annualised) cost per unit capacity and is charged once for the modelled horizon (24 h of objective-weighted snapshots); CAPEX and OPEX are only on the same time basis if that horizon is one year.",
